      "confidence": "candidate",
      "coverage_note": "A NestJS class decorator sits OUTSIDE the class it decorates: for @Controller() export class C, omega-typescript spans reference.decorator on the decorator name and definition.class from the class keyword, so the decorator is neither within the class nor does it carry it as definition.container. The decorator and the class are therefore joined on the artifact path, which is exact for the one-decorated-class-per-file layout the Nest CLI generates and over-attributes in a file that declares several classes."
