  "coverage": {
    "mode": "explicit-classified",
    "gaps": [
      "The JS/TS Packs publish no argument text, so a route URL, a controller prefix, a websocket message name, an @Inject token and the classes named in @UseGuards and friends are all unreachable; a Route, a MessageHandler and an EnhancerBinding are located by file and byte offset, not by the string they carry.",
      "@Module({ imports, controllers, providers, exports }) is an object literal inside a decorator call, and omega-typescript emits nothing for an identifier in an array literal, so the module graph -- which module provides what, which module imports which -- is not statable today. This is the largest single gap and it is a Pack question, recorded in the Framework's design note.",
      "A class decorator is a sibling of its class, not a child, once the class is exported -- which is how every Nest class is written -- so @Controller, @Injectable, @Module, @WebSocketGateway and @Catch cannot name their class by span. nestjs.class.role joins them on the artifact path instead and is exact only for one decorated class per file.",
      "custom and composed decorators require cross-file decorator-definition expansion before they can inherit Nest semantics",
      "runtime DI provider selection, dynamic modules (forRoot/forFeature) and container state remain runtime semantics"
    ]
  },
